    hanbi[smile]: …I'd like that too. I think I'd be better at it.
    hanbi: …An ordinary day, then. One we chose.
* [quiet] "I've started a lot of things the week before I left. I want this one to start on a day I'm staying."
    @rel hanbi trust+1
    hanbi: …Then we pick a day. One where nobody's leaving. I'd like that more than I can— no. I'd like that very much.
> He takes the new pencil from behind his ear. He tears the card along its fold, slowly, so that there isn't a ragged edge. *FUTURE* on one half, *LETTER* on the other.
hanbi[thinking]: …It was raining. The first time. It was twenty to four in the afternoon.
hanbi: …The first rain of spring. 15:40. This bench.
